.TH SAMU 1 "September 2026" "REM developer tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
samu \- execute a Ninja build description
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B samu
[-C dir] [-f build.ninja] [-n] [target ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B samu
is Samurai, a Ninja-compatible build executor. It reads a build graph and
starts the listed commands. On REM, the compiler, assembler and linker named
by the build graph must be available in PATH or named explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -C DIR
Change to DIR before reading the build graph.
.TP
.B -f FILE
Read FILE instead of the default build.ninja.
.TP
.B -n
Print commands without running them (dry run), when supported by the installed
build.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
samu -f build.ninja
samu -n -f build.ninja
samu -f build.ninja hello
.fi
.SH REM STATUS
Compilation of Samurai source and native executable qualification have had
separate blockers. Presence of this manual does not mean a working \fBsamu\fR
binary is installed. Check REM_SAMURAI_STATUS.md and qualify a real and
incremental build on the exact rootfs before depending on it.
.SH SEE ALSO
make(1), chibicc(1)
